+# V21: startup stage effect split
+
+New explicit `--startup-effect-routines TARGET` defaults to null/off and accepts only `first-medium-vehicle-0`, `first-low-day-1-on`, or `first-high-day-1-on`. It is mutually exclusive with legacy `--startup-routines`; CLI, canonical transforms, browser/build seal and receipts enforce this. The immutable V18–V20 packs and legacy eight-target module/core/actions remain unchanged. This new pack has41 sealed inputs, including tests.
+
+Exact Game/light source transforms reuse the original options object and already-read pass/stage/render clocks. Only the selected stage installs one shared ten-target stack: the original eight routines plus PBR._prepareEffect and the concrete engine instance's native createEffect. There is no Scene.render wrapper. Both native WebGPUEngine own and inherited ThinEngine origins are checked. PBR and direct Standard readiness ancestry can reach the engine row; foreign scenes/material branches are passthrough. The output does not inspect cache keys, claim hit/miss, or explain Standard internals with PBR spans.
+
+The distinct startup-only raw field is `startupStageEffects`. It contains fixed targets, phase rows with nullReturns/inclusiveMs/selfSelectedMs, original boundaries, renderer/generation, origin, installation/cleanup and partial/cap evidence. Limits remain16passes/304stages/8selected original renders/256KiB and the enclosing receipt remains2MiB. A genuinely ended stage with six valid frames can be complete; this is not the eight-frame entry schema. Unreached/aborted/overflow/foreign/error states remain partial. Rejected startup before observer installation omits the optional profile; a resolved enabled startup must include it.
+
+No render/readiness/GPU/original-clock/await/timer/scheduler/cache scan is added. Startup ready=false and legitimate pending preparation/shader-validation work are permitted. The existing source15 30s/90s limits, quality/coverage and scope/fence operations are preserved. These are synchronous diagnostic wall spans including observer/JIT/GC/scheduling, not GPU execution or a performance acceptance result.
+
+The ten-target core is byteexact from entry-effect-cost/helper/v19; the post-ready capture adapter is not used. The new stage adapter releases its caller-owned target transaction array immediately after constructor validation, so retained lower-core engine/PBR wrappers do not retain Game/Scene/engine. It also provides exact descriptor rollback, partial RTT registration rollback, owner/device/generation/abort guards, native frame progress, bounded phase/renderer registration and terminal scalar state.
+
+Only targeted light CPU regressions were run here. They execute the actual transformed Game options literal and original light state machine, native PBR/Standard/ThinEngine, WebGPU-origin installation without device work, nesting/null/falsy throws/Promise identity, caps, strict receipts, legacy compatibility, and retained-wrapper GC. RED and intermediate failures are preserved in the new startup-effect-v21 evidence; whole corpus/build/server/GPU remain pending with the coordinator/CAD resource window. Historical text below describes earlier packs.
+
 # V18: startup stage routines (diagnostika)
 
 Nová volba --startup-routines TARGET je výchozí null/vypnuto. Uzavřené cíle: first-medium-vehicle-0, first-low-day-1-on, first-high-day-1-on. Target je v canonical transforms.startupRoutines; browser/sidecar identity jej odvozuje a loadBuild ověřuje target i oba původní/transformed Game/light zdroje. Default-off nechává jejich bytes beze změny a nezakládá owner/hooks/čtení Game. Všechny takto aktivované běhy jsou diagnostic.
